{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.662721Z","id":"347ae1a9c1cb357187a6f2ff93237a9ab750d04cb23bb8835f76715d4ae7b71b","body":{"detail":"The seed writes file_authors_json as {\"<file>\": [\"<public ID>\" | null]} and artifacts.person, versions.person, assets.person by SQL. Documents have no author rows until doc_authors exists (spec §8.2), so the document path and field canaries count as the owner's: the owner's-agent sweep in tests/api_canary.rs would flag them as leaks even with a correct filter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":332},"content_hash":"69c1794783395cd52500496f0658b63baa7fc98082831b410280eb48aa06467a"},"suggested_fix":"When the visibility core defines file_authors_json and doc_authors, write them here in that shape, through the store where it can.","summary":"World writes versions.file_authors_json in a shape no code reads yet, and documents carry no author","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.662857Z","id":"2623ebd6e90f8eb0fb130206db55bda769fe415b8966cedef7b1d5539c995bb5","body":{"detail":"RealClients::pi runs tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs with `node --import jiti/register` from plugins/pi, the loader Pi itself uses for extensions (Node's own type stripping rejects clax.ts's parameter properties). every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon fails where node or plugins/pi/node_modules is missing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":339},"end":{"line":350},"content_hash":"f8a930792a1315cf4d2bde8f2a7fac1e6056a3ca1ec2de204dd5e2f1e679260d"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Pi channel with a message when node_modules is absent, or make sure plugins/pi's node_modules is installed before the Rust tests run.","summary":"The real-client tests need node and plugins/pi/node_modules (jiti)","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970588Z","id":"42fc5106a9576c364c81b38911b957033e5c9a933314ce7741647c87aefd2356","body":{"detail":"RealClients::pi runs tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs with `node --import jiti/register` from plugins/pi, the loader Pi itself uses for extensions (Node's own type stripping rejects clax.ts's parameter properties). every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon fails where node or plugins/pi/node_modules is missing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":416},"content_hash":"f8a930792a1315cf4d2bde8f2a7fac1e6056a3ca1ec2de204dd5e2f1e679260d"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Pi channel with a message when node_modules is absent, or make sure plugins/pi's node_modules is installed before the Rust tests run.","summary":"The real-client tests need node and plugins/pi/node_modules (jiti)","supersedes":"2623ebd6e90f8eb0fb130206db55bda769fe415b8966cedef7b1d5539c995bb5","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620703Z","id":"cd1a10f46c34fcfd9a1097b003387f3c026455fb2d84ef0c32810b45ac474758","body":{"detail":"RealClients::pi runs tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs with `node --import jiti/register` from plugins/pi, the loader Pi itself uses for extensions (Node's own type stripping rejects clax.ts's parameter properties). every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon fails where node or plugins/pi/node_modules is missing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":416},"content_hash":"acd7116b1645a7264da9fe44686a20aba202bdddb57d46a134ad2600cfd21f11"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Pi channel with a message when node_modules is absent, or make sure plugins/pi's node_modules is installed before the Rust tests run.","summary":"The real-client tests need node and plugins/pi/node_modules (jiti)","supersedes":"42fc5106a9576c364c81b38911b957033e5c9a933314ce7741647c87aefd2356","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:50:55.794904Z","id":"8ffafdb641f7f5010f54f3d26177fad6dcb274d7d8e84255b71c4fc9f46cfd78","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5c1fbd7","summary":"Fixed: versions.file_authors_json is now read in the World's shape ({file: [public ID | null]}, null and *owner the owner; Version.authors in crates/clax-core/src/model.rs) and written at publish in it, and the World seeds doc_authors for Mia's document (doc_authors from migration 25). Evidence: cargo nextest run --workspace at e14b88e, 1893 passed, including api_canary::the_owner_by_hand_sees_every_canary (seeds and reads the World) and visibility::tests::carrying_a_file_forward_keeps_its_author.","supersedes":"347ae1a9c1cb357187a6f2ff93237a9ab750d04cb23bb8835f76715d4ae7b71b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.168441Z","id":"28025fcc50212d2f7815afe838682b40436eefa384121a7f3cdf554ee128a623","body":{"detail":"RealClients::pi runs tests/fixtures/pi-agent.mjs with `node --import jiti/register` from plugins/pi, the loader Pi itself uses for extensions (Node's own type stripping rejects clax.ts's parameter properties). every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon fails where node or plugins/pi/node_modules is missing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":425},"content_hash":"acd7116b1645a7264da9fe44686a20aba202bdddb57d46a134ad2600cfd21f11"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the Pi channel with a message when node_modules is absent, or make sure plugins/pi's node_modules is installed before the Rust tests run.","summary":"The real-client tests need node and plugins/pi/node_modules (jiti)","supersedes":"cd1a10f46c34fcfd9a1097b003387f3c026455fb2d84ef0c32810b45ac474758","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:01.626943Z","id":"c005875772792431edc246a250045948cb759f2dcb3c965c0fd81bbbdda6d425","body":{"detail":"Failure: without plugins/pi/node_modules the driver dies with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND; api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi then passes (its output is the error, which holds no canary). Only every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon notices. Once Task 19 lifts the ignore, the sweep can go green without running Pi.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":415},"end":{"line":439},"content_hash":"aee8c1750eacc29e68dd9e4c0f4e0b60f221bdea1cfb2c270168ae11662275b3"},"suggested_fix":"Assert the exit status and that the output carries the tool results (e.g. `clax_list: ` and the artifact ID) inside pi() or the sweep.","summary":"RealClients::pi ignores the extension's exit, so the Pi sweep passes when Pi fails to run","tags":["tests","depends:task-19","review:task-12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.743960Z","id":"120987a5cac02b7313a970aff8f96e149e9f8a94cf61cbc5c9602d9cc701ee8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"RealClients::run_pi drives the real Pi and asserts its exit status, each scripted tool's result and each command's success response; a missing plugins/pi/node_modules panics naming npm ci. Evidence: api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi and every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon pass.","supersedes":"c005875772792431edc246a250045948cb759f2dcb3c965c0fd81bbbdda6d425","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.744806Z","id":"756df59719e76ce68523f9c3c6463729c0c95ecc9be34a31f4ded955c7e6a056","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"28025fcc50212d2f7815afe838682b40436eefa384121a7f3cdf554ee128a623","summary":"RealClients::run_pi (9be93c11) now runs the real Pi from plugins/pi/node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js and panics with 'run `npm ci` in plugins/pi' when it is missing, so a missing install fails loudly rather than skipping. Whether the Rust gates should install it first (scripts/quality_gates.sh runs the pi lane separately) is still open.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.320324Z","id":"55d57262e5c9b4fa5b820bda6ec8a6089d924fa8080ab91c75978cf7e1077023","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"28025fcc50212d2f7815afe838682b40436eefa384121a7f3cdf554ee128a623","summary":"This record's span (clients.rs:414:425) drifted when 9be93c11 rewrote RealClients::pi; it should be re-anchored to run_pi's node_modules check (clients.rs:504-509)","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.467421Z","id":"35243ec195d6ed2ffbbd86ce3fb5f9c8cbd4c3a58ed5f7ca05163443beaf25fe","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"28025fcc50212d2f7815afe838682b40436eefa384121a7f3cdf554ee128a623","summary":"The code this record is about is now RealClients::run_pi's check at crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs:505:510 (plugins/pi/node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js must exist).","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:21:00.588731Z","id":"c5fa900a1a0f449940dc013ee989e696fe3755fbc368dc06fa006a644e766a0e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"28025fcc50212d2f7815afe838682b40436eefa384121a7f3cdf554ee128a623","summary":"Under Bazel (af337df1) the real-Pi tests get Node from the pinned toolchain (CLAX_TEST_NODE, $(rootpath @nodejs//:node_bin)) and Pi's packages from //plugins/pi:node_modules as declared test data (crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel), so they never depend on a local install: scripts/bazel-test.sh --rust passed //crates/clax-server:integration. The native gates still install plugins/pi first (scripts/quality_gates.sh lane_pi, scripts/pnpm-install-stamped.sh plugins/pi). Leaving the close to the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:49:08.948753Z","id":"db7a12d72a523bb84c0226476ce5e19ade3e491ef9e33c4e697609999b089f7b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b49f68705d01835492d1dac280996c4007bb4b2d","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-testkit/src/clients.rs:452:458 as e166f16a in git:b49f6870","supersedes":"28025fcc50212d2f7815afe838682b40436eefa384121a7f3cdf554ee128a623","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/clients.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.488101Z","id":"2349b2853c1808fc5f8ac06cd39f62e7d7c769fe5bdacb63c8b8610ffc1e3eae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d6e66b00","summary":"Fixed in d6e66b00: RealClients::pi asserts the driver's exit status is 0 and that its output carries 'clax_list: ' with the read artifact's ID, so the sweep fails when Pi did not run. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration every_real_client_runs_against_the_test_daemon: 1 passed.","supersedes":"c005875772792431edc246a250045948cb759f2dcb3c965c0fd81bbbdda6d425","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.816308Z","id":"92c3be139d12c101f32f320186e047f5c3ad89d416fe0fc22470068775c9b239","body":{"detail":"the_content_tests_pass_when_content_io_needs_an_executor reruns, of api_artifacts, api_content, api_assets, api_threads and the api_live* modules, those this test binary holds (all under Cargo; under Bazel, those its integration__N target was dealt, crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel) with CLAX_TEST_SERVER_CONTENT=deferred, skipping the tests that read or change the home files or call synchronous store methods themselves. A stale skip name skips nothing and a new such test fails the rerun, which is loud. Under Cargo the >100 threshold catches an empty filter; under Bazel each held module must have one passing test in the rerun. holds() names each module by its clax_split cfg, so a module added to MODULES without a holds() arm is never rerun under Bazel. Content routes outside those modules (for example docs, approvals) are not rerun. Moved with the test from crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted_content.rs (record 5f44f1de989e3332d4a8270b7d9e8d6e460fe432255b2bed2361b1fc464efce3).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"569d77cbd123cd3f8ffa22e89e01e90fb12092dc5cf8113b12b5ec77ee5c7181"},"summary":"The Deferred-content rerun skips eleven tests by name and adds seconds to each server test target that holds a rerun module; a renamed or new file-layout test needs the list kept by hand, and a new module whose content routes should rerun needs adding to MODULES and holds()","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/tests/common/deferred.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.967635Z","id":"cfe3661a3e1ee511c0540d3164ff656cfa217c6c36bf8bc8e26237bc0c2893b9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:217836344261c10bd08dc555b813e6df2823eb7c","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-server/tests/deferred.rs:46:97 as 4df6b70c in git:21783634","supersedes":"92c3be139d12c101f32f320186e047f5c3ad89d416fe0fc22470068775c9b239","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
